 know blatantly pushing link and  you know it's pretty easy to see what  i'm up to and stuff well yeah it is easy  to see because it's obvious  uh i enjoy doing these videos and  interacting with people but i wouldn't  do them if it weren't for the fact that  i'm hoping to attract people to link i  mean that's why i do them but that  doesn't mean that i don't believe in  link why do i ever get involved i've  been in the lumber business all my life  i don't really need it  i believe in it i believe there's a  better way of learning languages and so  i have committed an awful lot of time  to this project and we have invested uh  obviously money and uh and i believe in  it  and and it's my passion what's wrong  with that what's wrong with talking  about things that are interesting uh uh  of interest to me uh there's no hidden  agenda here it's pretty clear some  people may say that i mentioned link too  often whatever i'll do what i want  someone else can make videos and talk  about what they want to talk about  now getting back to korean  i praised the colloquial learning korean  and i think the main reason is because  it was smaller than the other books  but i have now found having gone back to  it that yeah i can read through the  chapters 1 to 20 and i kind of half  start to remember what i had learned  before  but i couldn't listen to the cds anymore  because they're full of english  and i can't stand it uh you know first  of all they explain to you in english  what you're about to hear which  really annoys me  then they give you vocabulary with  english  explanations and then they ask you  questions plea and please answer in  korean and i find all of this stuff very  very annoying  so i was very happy that  hyunwu sun or i guess korean style sun  hyun wu  who has a website called talk to me in  korean  agreed to share  these dialogues in our link library the  dialogues are called talk to me in  korean they are tremendous intermediate  learning material tremendous the sound  quality is excellent  it consists of either hyun wu or someone  else usually there's a male and a female  it could be two females  and they talk about light subjects it  could be um  you know it could be bookstores whatever  i had bookstores lazy people  um  hmm  stress dealing with stress uh exercise  all these subjects talking about  everything and nothing really but in a  very pleasant way  natural  unscripted just two people having a  conversation but they managed to repeat  words over and over again so it's very  good for the learner  uh it's great listening even if i don't  understand it all i don't mind listening  again and again  and then of course i read it on link and  i look up the words that i don't  understand  and one of the things that i find quite  interesting with korean is that  with so many words you don't find a  satisfactory explanation in the  dictionary  part of it is because there are a lot of  words perhaps words that come from  chinese  that can have seven or eight meanings so  you don't know which one applies to this  particular context  or for some reason sometimes the  dictionaries just turn up ridiculous  uh  meaningless  definitions so  but you know what i don't mind this and  i think this is a good exercise they  should they should i think they should  do this in classes they should give  people dictionaries full of meaningless  uh  you know or 15 different definitions  and make them realize that  that  you know the language you're not going  to nail it down and even if they were  what looked to be the real meaning it  you're still not going to nail it down  so the fact that things are a little  fuzzier in korean  it just makes me want to listen more  often i'm more i'm keen to hear more and  more  of of content in korean because i know  it's eventually all going to fall into  place because the koreans make sense  when they talk to each other so  therefore eventually korean's going to  make sense to me  but  as i said on my blog post it's kind of  like a you know a beautiful woman she's  not gonna  make you aware of of of everything and  let you see everything right away you've  got to put in the time you got to put in  the effort and gradually you'll get to  know  the language  uh so i'm really enjoying korean from  that point of view um  also because we now have our our uh  again plugging link we have our app our  new app on ipod i'm able to do a a lot  of my reading  listening  i can review my saved words highlight  words in the text  on my  on my ipod app i can review my  flashcards i can even review my links of  the day that get emailed to me they also  line up in this app so i mean i can do a  lot of stuff i i had the meeting today i  was this gentleman was actually i met  with a canadian minister of government  to try to talk to him about  link and of course politicians are  always busy so i was uh you know left to  wait there but i was just as happy as  could be going through my  my uh korean on my little ipod shuffle  so that also has made the korean fun but  i am enjoying it and i think i'll  probably spend a month or so on the sort  of lighter intermediate stuff here talk  to me in korean i don't know how many  episodes there are i will find out  and then i'll move into heavier content  where  to some extent i'll have an advantage  because there will be a lot more uh  words that are based on chinese  characters and so i will have a lot of  that vocabulary from my chinese  so yeah i'm enjoying it the biggest  problem i'm gonna have with korean is i  set myself a challenge to see  um you know how much i can do between  now and december and i want to try to  have a conversation with someone in  december  but i'm going to portugal in october so  i also don't want to neglect my  portuguese i'm actually going to be  giving some uh conferences to to  language teachers in portugal before  that i have a conference in germany so i  do at some point have to refresh my  german  then because it's my 65th birthday my  wife and i are gonna spend  three weeks in sardinia  uh  my older boy and family are gonna come  over from england because they have  holidays at that time at least for one  week and then we're going to spend  another two weeks and then i want to  maybe drive through italy back up to  france or fly home but  so italia is going to be there and in  all of that i'm going to have to  maintain my korean studies  so that  in december i can actually carry on a  conversation in korea we will see how it  goes meanwhile thank you very much to uh  for the wonderful content you and your  team have created and talked to me in  korean thank you very much bye for now
 

